zoe lee: MerchantConnect wants a 10-day POC. Requirements: websocket streaming of incremental JSON rows, tool/function calls to payments.lookup, client-side ack for backpressure, and hosted + dedicated pricing for steady 50k tokens/day. They also attached an infosec questionnaire.
mahesh iyer: Recommended pattern: NDJSON over ws with a small envelope: {"t":"row","id":123,"p":{...}} or {"t":"tool","id":123,"name":"payments.lookup","res":{...}}. Keep each message as a complete JSON object so frontends don't need to buffer arrays.
ronnie: Backpressure: emit small rows and honor ack frames from client. We support sending server-side "pause" signals or switch to micro-batching under load. Also suggest heartbeat frames.
zoe lee: Can we show an example SDK snippet (minimal) to include in SOW? Need node + python.
mahesh iyer: Node minimal:
const s = await Redwood.stream.connect({key:process.env.RW});
s.on('message', m => { const o = JSON.parse(m); if(o.t==='row') render(o.id,o.p); if(o.t==='tool') handleTool(o.id,o.res); });
// client ack
s.send(JSON.stringify({t:'ack',lastId:42}));
Python minimal:
ws = connect_stream(key=os.getenv('RW'))
for msg in ws:
  o = json.loads(msg)
  if o['t']=='row': render(o['id'], o['p'])
  if o['t']=='tool': apply_tool(o['id'], o['res'])
  # send ack every 20 rows
  if should_ack(): ws.send(json.dumps({'t':'ack','lastId':o['id']}))
cassie_sales: Procurement wants hosted trial (30d) + dedicated 3mo POC numbers. Ballpark hosted: ~$0.003/token (trial discount possible). Dedicated: starting pool ~$24k/mo with ~30-45% lower effective token price after commit (need finance to finalize).
zoe lee: Security quick notes: SOC2 yes, SAML SSO supported, IP allowlist, audit logs. BYOK requires Private. For hosted demo we can provide isolated project + ephemeral keys + audit trails. If they need KMS we recommend Private POC (10-14 business days).
infra-bot: ephemeral keys created: rw-ephemeral-3cde (72h)
mahesh iyer: Actions: 1) Mahesh to produce 1-page hosted POC runbook + sample NDJSON schema (tomorrow). 2) Cassie to send ballpark pricing spreadsheet (EOD). 3) Zoe to request SAML metadata + questionnaire answers and preferred start date.
